# Route Interfaces

This Livebook defines one exact route and uses the Signal and live-call helpers
that Jido generates for it.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define The Route

```elixir
defmodule RouteInterfaces.SetStatus do
  use Jido.Action,
    name: "route_interfaces_set_status",
    schema: Zoi.object(%{status: Zoi.enum([:open, :closed])})

  @impl Jido.Action
  def run(%{status: status}, %{agent_state: state}) do
    {:ok, %{state | status: status}}
  end
end

defmodule RouteInterfaces.Order do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "route_interfaces_order"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{status: Zoi.enum([:open, :closed]) |> Zoi.default(:open)})
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/route-interfaces"

    route "order.status.set", RouteInterfaces.SetStatus do
      define :set_status, args: [:status]
    end
  end
end
```

A generated interface requires an exact route with no match predicate. This
keeps one helper tied to one executable target.

## Construct A Signal

```elixir
{:ok, signal} = RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status_signal(:closed)

%{
  type: signal.type,
  source: signal.source,
  data: signal.data
}
```

The bang form, `set_status_signal!/1`, returns the Signal or raises a validation
error.

## Add Envelope And Input Data

```elixir
{:ok, signal} =
  RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status_signal(
    :closed,
    input: %{request_id: "req-1"},
    signal: [subject: "order-7"]
  )

{signal.data.request_id, signal.subject}
```

Do not provide the same input key both positionally and through `input:`.

## Use The Live Helper

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()

{:ok, order} =
  Jido.start_agent(
    Jido.default_instance(),
    RouteInterfaces.Order,
    id: "order-7"
  )

{:ok, committed} =
  RouteInterfaces.Order.set_status(
    order,
    :closed,
    context: %{actor: "reviewer"},
    timeout: 5_000
  )

committed.state.status
```

The live helper constructs the same Signal and calls `Jido.AgentServer.call/3`.

## Stop The Example

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(Jido.default_instance(), order)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

See [Signals, Commands, And Routes](signals-commands-and-routes.md) for route
selection rules.
